multiplication by r is a linear transformation on the Z-module R, and we write Tr(r) for the
trace of that linear transformation. The discriminant of a n-ic ring with Z-module basis ζi
is the determinant of the matrix with i, j entry Tr(ζi ζj ) (which is easily seen to not depend
on the choice of basis).

