   327	## 6. Consequences for a sextic with exactly three nodes
   328	
   329	The affine condition strengthens the conditional kill.  By §5, `a` and `b`
   330	have no common affine zero, since every such zero would be a non-nodal
   331	singularity of `F`.  Let `AA,BB` be their degree-two and degree-three
