   333	would occur at least squared in `FF`, contrary to the reduced irreducible
   334	sextic.  Bezout therefore gives total intersection number six.
   335	
   336	Every common zero lies on `FF=0`.  There is no affine one, and the sextic has
   337	only the point `Q` at infinity, so
